&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 1&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49536529</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 14:10:21 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: UluP Desktop – your file system as a node-based canvas with AI</title><link>https://www.ulupstudio.com/desktop</link><description>&lt;p&gt;I built a Windows desktop app that represents your files and folders as nodes on a visual canvas instead of a traditional tree view. Drag positions persist across sessions, real thumbnails for images, and you can draw arbitrary connections between files that don't share a folder hierarchy.&lt;p&gt;The part I found genuinely interesting to build: it exposes a local MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that Claude Code can connect to — so you can control the file system through natural conversation. Since it's a stdio-based local server (not a hosted one), there's no API billing involved if you already have a Claude subscription — the conversation itself uses your existing quota.&lt;p&gt;Built with Electron + React + ReactFlow. Auto-updates via a generic feed (had some infrastructure constraints that ruled out GitHub Releases). Free.&lt;p&gt;ulupstudio.com/desktop&lt;/p&gt;
